Z||000000||ponya||10-19-2000||04:39 PM||||I guess that this will go against everyone's grain, but has anyone tried any of these oil leak sealants that are on the market? I have a rear main seal that drips a drop or two over the course of a week. Right now I don't have the money to have it repaired or even repair it myself. I always have to watch where I park it, even though the leak is small, it's still a leak and makes spots. I thought I would try one of those leak stopper products as a temp. fix. Any ideas or opinions appreciated.  thanks, Bob||||reg||5
Z||000001||theogre||10-19-2000||05:15 PM||||Those sealers my help with leaking gaskets. They usually won't work on shaft seals like a main.<P>The seal itself isn't all that expensive. It's just that you have to take everything apart to get to it.||||reg||1
